Package: imbalanceKit
Type: Package
Title: Resampling Methods and Tools for Imbalanced Classification
Version: 0.1.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    c(person("Fatih", "Saglam", email = "saglamf89@gmail.com", 
    role = c("aut", "cre"), 
    comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-2084-2008")))
Description: A collection of resampling methods for class imbalance in
    classification problems. Includes the oversampling methods SMOTE with
    boosting (SMOTEWB) by F. Sağlam and M. A. Cengiz (2022)
    <doi:10.1016/j.eswa.2022.117023>, Markov chain SMOTE (MCSMOTE) by
    F. Sağlam and M. A. Cengiz (2025) <doi:10.1016/j.asoc.2025.113906>,
    uncertainty guided oversampling (UGO) by F. Sağlam and M. A. Cengiz (2026)
    <doi:10.1016/j.knosys.2026.115886>, and bi-directional SMOTE (BiSMOTE) by
    F. Sağlam and U. Yamak (2027) <doi:10.1016/j.eswa.2026.134648>, and the
    data relocation approach DatRel by F. Sağlam (2025)
    <doi:10.1007/s10994-025-06755-8>, together
    with commonly used alternatives such as SMOTE, ADASYN, Borderline-SMOTE,
    Safe-Level-SMOTE, geometric SMOTE, random oversampling and undersampling.
    The methods share the same interface: they take a feature matrix and a
    factor class variable and return the resampled data together with the
    synthetic samples.
Depends: R (>= 4.0.0)
Imports: 
    stats,
    utils,
    FNN,
    rpart,
    Rfast
